From: FP3 camera work
Subject: [PATCH] camera: re-apply the autofocus mode once the viewfinder streams

The autofocus mode is a camera control, and a control only reaches the
camera while it is streaming - a mode set before the first frame goes to
a pipeline with no request to carry it and is lost. The mode was set once
at start-up, before streaming, and never resent (the setting does not
change on its own), so the camera kept hunting continuously even with
autofocus switched off. Re-apply it each time the viewfinder reaches
Ready, by when frames, and so requests to carry the control, are flowing.
--- a/src/widgets/camera.rs
+++ b/src/widgets/camera.rs
@@ -397,8 +397,23 @@
             self.viewfinder.connect_state_notify(glib::clone!(
                 #[weak]
                 obj,
-                move |_| {
+                move |viewfinder| {
                     obj.update_state();
+
+                    // The autofocus mode is a camera control, and a control
+                    // only reaches the camera while it is streaming: a mode set
+                    // before the first frame goes to a pipeline with no request
+                    // to carry it and is lost. The setting does not change on
+                    // its own afterwards, so nothing resends it - which left
+                    // the camera hunting continuously even with autofocus
+                    // switched off, the mode set once at start-up never having
+                    // landed. Re-apply it each time the viewfinder reaches
+                    // Ready, by when frames - and so requests to carry the
+                    // control - are flowing.
+                    if matches!(viewfinder.state(), aperture::ViewfinderState::Ready) {
+                        let settings = gio::Settings::new(config::APP_ID);
+                        viewfinder.set_autofocus(settings.boolean("autofocus"));
+                    }
                 }
             ));
 
